=== MODIFICATIONS ===

Files imported from Open Science (commit d8f11e34) are MODIFIED per
Apache-2.0 §4. Modifications include:

- Rebranding: Lumen Science Desktop namespacing and brand assets.
- Authority removal: all execution paths (ACP runtime, notebook kernel executor,
  compute SSH/SCP runner, job poller, agent framework backends, permission
  broker) replaced with descriptive no-op stubs. Stubbed modules throw or
  return CANCELLED; no TS executor or SSH/SCP process can be launched.
- Desktop bridge: lumen-acp-bridge.ts added for Rust Lumen SessionActor
  integration (ACP loopback). Bridge orchestrates lumen binary lifecycle;
  Electron main does NOT execute science tools directly.
- Connector catalog: UI reused; Rust adapters remain authoritative.
- Notebook: kernel-executor.ts, runtime-service.ts, and notebook/ipc.ts
  are STUBBED — no Python/R kernel execution through Electron.
  Actual notebook execution requires wiring Rust KernelAdapter (follow-on).
- Reviewer: reviewer/ipc.ts is STUBBED — no runReview orchestration
  through Electron. Reviewer verdict routing through SessionActor
  is DESIGNED as follow-on work.
- Compute: ssh-runner.ts, scp-runner.ts, job-poller.ts, compute-service.ts,
  job-dispatcher.ts, harvest-engine.ts, compute/ipc.ts, and
  compute-approval-broker.ts are all STUBBED — no SSH/SCP/job execution
  through Electron. Actual remote compute requires Rust ToolAdapter
  integration (follow-on).
- Desktop bridge: lumen-acp-bridge.ts added for Rust Lumen SessionActor
  integration (ACP loopback). Bridge exports installIpcGuard which is
  wired into ipcMain at startup — BANNED channels are blocked and acp:call
  routes to Rust binary. Bridge orchestrates lumen binary lifecycle.

